+- **Lists and caches.** Every save the server accepts makes the editor read the Loops list and the loop's detail again (`refreshLoopAfterWrite`). This includes the save sent on leaving the editor and saves whose editor has closed. A publish answer also refreshes the loop's versions and webhook endpoints. A read that started before the write is cancelled first, and its answer is never stored, even when it is a first load. Nothing is copied from a write's own answer, so an older write cannot replace a newer snapshot, and list order, other loops and run summaries come from the server. A refused or failed save refreshes nothing. A failed read stays in its query's error state. Publishing does not re-run the open draft's API checks, which are keyed by its draft token; other loops' checks are marked stale without being run, because a subloop reference reads this loop's published version.
